---
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/words-per-state-dark.svg?raw';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/words-per-state-light.svg?raw';
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={680}
  caption="UI words per screen state under the browser benchmark's counting rules (order data, keycaps, and two-word symptom tiles excluded). Each state's final count is locked as its exact CI budget; training lesson states carry a separate 12-word coaching ceiling."
>
  A broken-axis horizontal bar chart comparing UI word counts across nine screen
  states before redesign or the final trim pass against their locked CI budgets
  today, with a vertical dashed line at the 15-word rule cap. Tape playing
  dropped from 148 words to 8 (-95 percent), the Fail symptom picker from 34 to
  3, Order ready from 29 to 3, Round 2 ready from 24 to 13, Exception (note
  open) from 21 to 15, Can't inspect (note open) from 20 to 15, Inspection
  result from 18 to 15, Already inspected from 25 to 17, and Round 2 tape from
  25 to 18 (the last two include a 2-to-3-word prior-inspection strip).
</Diagram>
